Internova Sales Analytics Dashboard

Project Overview

This project focuses on analysing Internova's sales data to evaluate business performance, understand customer purchasing behaviour and identify opportunities for revenue growth.

Using Microsoft Power BI, I transformed sales data into an interactive dashboard that provides insights into sales trends, customer retention, product category performance, customer segmentation, geographical distribution and shipping preferences.

The objective was to move beyond presenting sales figures and provide actionable business recommendations that could support better decision-making.

Tools and Technologies

- Microsoft Power BI
- Power Query
- DAX (Data Analysis Expressions)

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

The analysis focused on the following metrics:

KPI| Result
Total Sales| $2.26M
Total Customers| 793
Repeat Customers| 780
Repeat Customer Rate| 98.36%
Average Sales per Customer| $2,850
Average Order Value| $459.48

Key Business Insights

1. Customer Retention

Out of 793 customers, 780 are repeat buyers, representing a 98.36% repeat customer rate.

Business Recommendation: Strengthen customer retention through loyalty programmes, personalised promotions and referral incentives.

2. Product Category Performance

Technology leads revenue generation with approximately $836K in sales, while Office Supplies records the highest order frequency.

Business Recommendation: Explore cross-selling and product bundling opportunities to increase average order value.

3. Customer Segmentation

The Consumer segment contributes 50.79% of total sales, followed by Corporate at 30.44% and Home Office at 18.78%.

Business Recommendation: Maintain Consumer customer engagement while developing targeted purchasing incentives for Corporate and Home Office customers.

4. Geographical Performance

Sales activity is concentrated in the West and East regions, with cities such as New York City, Los Angeles, Philadelphia, San Francisco and Seattle among the leading contributors.

Business Recommendation: Investigate opportunities to improve market penetration in underperforming geographical regions.

5. Sales Trends and Shipping Performance

Sales peak in Q4 after a slight decline in Q2. Standard Class dominates shipping preferences, accounting for 59.79% of orders.

Business Recommendation: Improve inventory planning ahead of Q4 and investigate opportunities to optimise shipping operations.

Project Deliverables

- Interactive Power BI sales dashboard.
- Customer analytics and sales performance analysis.
- Business insights and actionable recommendations.
- Executive sales performance report.

Key Takeaway

This project demonstrates how data analytics can help businesses understand customer behaviour, evaluate sales performance, identify growth opportunities and make informed business decisions.

Rather than focusing solely on what happened, the analysis explores what the findings mean for the business and what actions management can take.
